  "finalReport": "## Final Policy Report\n\nStarting policy reached a 60% pass rate against the 40-borrower eval set, with an estimated default risk of 7% among approved loans. Over 4 iterations the loop identified three systematic misjudgments — young businesses rejected on age alone, risky high-debt borrowers approved on credit score alone, and collateral-backed borrowers rejected without a manual-review path — and applied one bounded threshold change per pattern.\n\n**Final pass rate: 90%** (target ≥ 85%)\n**Final default risk estimate: 4%** (target ≤ 5%)\n\n### What changed\n- Minimum business age: 24 → 18 months\n- Maximum debt-to-income: 0.42 → 0.39\n- Minimum monthly cash flow: $12,000 → $10,000\n- Collateral review path: disabled → enabled for collateral ratio ≥ 0.6\n\n### What's still failing\n4 of 40 cases (10%) remain unresolved. All four share high industry risk combined with a prior default, but pass every quantitative threshold in the policy. No bounded threshold change could catch these without also rejecting comparable good-faith borrowers — flagged for follow-up as a candidate for a composite risk signal rather than a single-field threshold.\n\nUnderwriteLoop does not approve these borrowers, or any borrower. It stress-tests the policy that will.",
